      "writtenOn": "2021-05-12T23:39:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "With regards to VCN over WiFi: VCN is meant to be a network abstraction that is only ever exposed as CELLULAR. Not checking location for VCN networks would be wai",
      "parentUuid": "61632186_733732cf",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 9087,
        "startChar": 81,
        "endLine": 9088,
        "endChar": 57
      },
      "revId": "940b08532f76fa58c99257b6a37beb86571a1935",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9c8ac862_4d60c837",
        "filename": "services/core/java/com/android/server/ConnectivityService.java",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 9088,
      "author": {
        "id": 1015428
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-05-13T11:41:43Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "But in practice it\u0027s possible to know whether you have a VCN running, and we\u0027ll want to make this clearer in the future, including whether it runs over WiFi. The VCN is meant to be a network abstraction of a *carrier*, not of cellular, and we should not make that confusion.\n\nAt this point I am unconvinced we should let apps listen to this for non-wifi networks without the location permission. If you want to listen to these callbacks, you should be prepared to have the permission and to be blamed for it.",
      "parentUuid": "fef90c4d_8e8ab4e0",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 9087,
        "startChar": 81,
        "endLine": 9088,
        "endChar": 57
      },
      "revId": "940b08532f76fa58c99257b6a37beb86571a1935",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
